{
  "esm": "1.0.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "OpenAQConsumerE2E",
    "description": "End-to-end consumer fixture for the pure-IO data-loader migration (RFC pure-io-data-loaders §6/§7; bead esm-3nc.6). A downstream consumer model that {\"ref\"}-includes the migrated single-component model components/earthsci_data/openaq.esm as the subsystem `aq`, then re-exposes the regridded air-quality field as the observed `pm25_consumed ~ aq.pm25`.\n\nPurpose: prove that a consumer file which references a migrated single-component model RESOLVES through the canonical ESS runner (the consumer's ref resolves to openaq.esm, which at esm 1.0.0 holds BOTH the OpenAQ model and the OpenAQ_obs `data_sources` entry that model consumes — the standalone openaq_loader.esm is gone, because a data source is no longer a component and `data_sources` no longer counts toward a file's top-level system count, so a single file carrying a model and its sources is still mountable by {\"ref\"}) and that the per-variable REGRID intent (cell_average + missing_value 0.0) survives the migration, identical to the pre-migration inline OpenAQ pipeline whose co-located data_loaders.OpenAQ_obs.regridding carried fill_value 0.0.\n\nThis fixture is exercised by test/e2e_consumer_regrid_check.py (esm-3nc.6). It is intentionally NOT placed under components/** or lib/**, so the run_esm_inline_tests.py gate and the Julia inline-test discovery do not auto-walk it — the model carries no self-contained numeric inline tests because air-quality loaders require external station data (downstream consumer-repo concern per AGENTS.md §2).",
    "authors": [
      "EarthSciModels migration (esm-3nc.6)"
    ],
    "created": "2026-06-25T00:00:00Z"
  },
  "models": {
    "OpenAQConsumerE2E": {
      "variables": {
        "lon": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "rad",
          "default": 0.0,
          "description": "Longitude of the consumer grid point (radians). Shares the name `lon` with the OpenAQ subsystem parameter so the two unify at flatten time, exactly as the migrated OpenAQ model unifies `lon` with its own loader subsystem."
        },
        "lat": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "rad",
          "default": 0.0,
          "description": "Latitude of the consumer grid point (radians). Shares the name `lat` with the OpenAQ subsystem parameter."
        },
        "pm25_consumed": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "kg/m^3",
          "description": "PM2.5 concentration consumed from the migrated OpenAQ regridding model via the subsystem reference. Pass-through of aq.pm25, which in components/earthsci_data/openaq.esm is the OpenAQ parameter `pm25` carrying `update: {kind: \"data\", source: \"OpenAQ_obs\", from: {file_variable: ...}}` — at esm 1.0.0 a consumed data field is a PARAMETER on the consuming model, not a subsystem observed (the 0.x form was OpenAQ.pm25 ~ obs.pm25 with `obs` a loader subsystem). Units kg/m^3 match the migrated model's exposed pm25 field and the pre-migration inline OpenAQ.pm25."
        }
      },
      "subsystems": {
        "aq": {
          "ref": "../../../components/earthsci_data/openaq.esm"
        }
      },
      "equations": [
        {
          "lhs": "pm25_consumed",
          "rhs": "aq.pm25"
        }
      ]
    }
  }
}
